CHEYENNE WYOMING:
Section1.
That various sections of Chapter 5.04, Business Licenses Generally, of
Title 5, Business Licenses and Regulations, of the code of the Cityof Cheyenne, Wyoming, are
hereby amended asset out in this ordinance.
5.04.100
Suspension and revocation.
In the event the mayor orcity couneil city clerk deems a license or permit should be
suspended or revoked, the following procedure shall be followed:
A.The licensee or permittee will be notified, in writing, by certified mail, by the city
clerk atleast seven daysprior to the action contemplated, stating thereasons therefor.
B.Upon receipt of the notice, the licensee or permittee may request a hearing. The
request must be in writing and received by the city clerk within seven days of receipt of the
notice.Failure on the part of the licensee or permittee to request a hearing in writing within the
specified time period shall be deemed a waiver of the licensee's or permittee's right to request a
hearing.
C.If a hearing is requested and received by the city clerk within the specified time
period, the city elerk will schedule a hearing before the governing body and notify the licensee of
perrnittee, in writing, by certified mail of the date, time and place of the meeting the matter shall
follow the provisions of Chapter 2.92, Administrative Hearing Procedure.
D.At -the-hearing, the licensee/permittee and other interested parties may be in
attendance to present any information relative-to the proposed suspension or revocation of the
license or permit. The hearing, deliberations and notification of decision regarding the
suspension-or revocation-will be-conducted pursuant-to-the Wyoming Administrative Procedure
Aet, Wyo. Stat. Sections 16-1-103, et seq. The city clerk will notify the licensee/permittee-in
writing, by certified mail, of the governing body decision as the result of the-hearing.
5.04.110
Emergency suspension.
If the mayor city clerk finds that cause exists for an immediate suspension or revocation
of a license or permit, he or she may enter an order for immediate suspension of same. The
licensee or permittee, upon notice of suspension or revocation, may request an immediate
SeetionS.04.100pursuant to Chapter2.92, Administrative Hearing Procedure.
